Upstream NOTICE (verbatim, the part relevant to the code taken):

  heic-rs is an independent implementation of ISO/IEC 23008-12 (HEIF) and of the
  decoding process described in Recommendation ITU-T H.265 | ISO/IEC 23008-2
  (High Efficiency Video Coding).

  No code was taken from any GPL, LGPL or AGPL licensed decoder. The algorithms
  are written from the published specification text. Permissively licensed Rust
  projects were consulted for cross-checking header syntax only, with no code
  copied:

    * rust_h265    (MIT OR Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/roticv/rust_h265
    * scuffle-h265 (MIT OR Apache-2.0)  NAL and parameter set header parsing

  This crate does not grant any patent licence to the HEVC standard itself.

Modifications by the Specular project (2026-10), under the same licence terms
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). No code from other decoders (libde265, ffmpeg, HM,
oxideav) was copied; they were used as test oracles and for behaviour only.

  * Layout: `src/hevc/` became this crate's `src/`; `crate::hevc::` paths,
    the `no_std` attribute, the `bench` feature and the seam into the
    heic-rs container error type were removed. `std` is used (threads,
    cancellation). `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` kept.
  * Chroma fixes: `cbf_cb`/`cbf_cr` are parsed for 4x4 transform units in
    4:4:4 (7.3.8.8); Table 8-3 (4:2:2 chroma mode mapping) corrected; the
    4:2:2 parent chroma cbf is the OR of both sub-block flags. The frame
    reports the chroma bit depth separately (`Frame::bit_depth_chroma`).
  * Deblocking: the chroma QP offset used for chroma edges is the PPS offset
    only (8.7.2.5.5, cQpPicOffset), not PPS + slice.
  * Multilayer: NAL units with nuh_layer_id > 0 are ignored and the
    SPS/PPS multilayer extension flags are tolerated (base layer decoded).
    `explicit_rdpcm_enabled_flag` (inter-only syntax) is accepted.
  * Slice-data driver rewritten (`decode/mod.rs`, `decode/slice_data.rs`):
    dependent slice segments (header inheritance, context, StatCoeff and
    QP carry-over); context initialisation per 9.3.1 with WPP storage keyed
    by CTB so slices that start or end mid-row (WPP_D) decode; StatCoeff
    synchronised with the WPP contexts (9.3.2.4); substreams bounded by
    their entry points.
  * Error tolerance and concealment (`decode/conceal.rs`): parameter sets
    that fail to parse are dropped, not fatal; non-IRAP and undecodable
    slice headers are skipped; a slice segment that fails is cut at the
    failing CTU and every CTU it no longer covers is concealed from the
    sample row above / column to the left (else mid-grey), with the
    in-loop filters disabled on it. The picture is returned with a count
    of concealed CTUs instead of failing; only a picture with no decoded
    CTU is an error.
  * Wavefront-parallel decode (`decode/wpp.rs`) under a thread budget:
    workers claim CTU rows, decode into row bands with a one-row halo,
    wait on the row above (two-CTU lag) through a mutex/condvar progress
    table, and merge into the picture. Deblocking runs on row bands cut
    at an 8k + 4 row above each CTB row (luma and chroma as separate
    jobs, filtering in place through disjoint row slices); SAO runs per
    component and CTB row from a snapshot of the deblocked picture. New
    `PlaneMut` row views and `Plane::split_rows` in picture.rs, and
    `loop_filters` in filter/mod.rs. Cancellation (`Error::Cancelled`)
    is polled per CTU in the parallel path and per CTU row in the serial
    one. Output is identical for every thread count, including on
    damaged streams.
  * New `hvcc` module: hvcC record parsing and length-prefixed NAL
    splitting (tolerant of truncation); `Options`/`Decoded` API with the
    VUI video_signal_type (`Signal`) returned to the caller.
  * Removed unused helpers (`Cabac::restart_at`, `Plane::new/row/row_mut`).
  * Range extensions (H.265 7.3.8.12, 8.6, 9.3), written from the spec
    text: cross-component prediction (log2_res_scale_abs_plus1 /
    res_scale_sign_flag, 8.6.6); implicit RDPCM for intra transform-skip
    and transquant-bypass blocks (8.6.5/8.6.8) with sign hiding and the
    intra boundary filter disabled as specified; transform-skip rotation
    limited to 4x4 blocks and applied to bypass residuals; persistent
    Rice adaptation without the cap of 4 and with the spec sbType;
    cabac_bypass_alignment (escapeDataPresent, ivlCurrRange = 256 before
    the bypass bins); extended_precision_processing (CoeffMin/Max from
    log2TransformRange, dequant and transform bdShift, 64-bit inverse
    transform and transform skip, limited k-th order Exp-Golomb
    binarisation 9.3.3.4); bit depths up to 16. log2_sao_offset_scale is
    validated against the bit depth. Chroma intra mode lookup in 4:4:4
    NxN CUs uses the prediction block that contains the chroma TU.
    Remaining refusals (Error::Unsupported): separate colour planes,
    3D/SCC extensions, pictures using more than one PPS; inter slices and
    non-IRAP pictures only through `VideoDecoder` (below), not as stills.
  * Inter decoding (H.265 7.3.8.6, 8.3, 8.5, 9.3), written from the spec
    text: RPS (short- and long-term, inter-RPS prediction), POC, DPB with
    output bumping, merge and AMVP candidates with TMVP and MV scaling,
    8-tap luma / 4-tap chroma interpolation, default and explicit
    weighted (bi-)prediction, the P/B CABAC context tables, boundary
    strength 1/2 for inter edges, deblocking and SAO on inter pictures.
    `VideoDecoder` decodes an access-unit sequence in output order.
  * Worker threads are named per Specular's scheme (specular-thread):
    `dec-hevc-N` (frame pool), `dec-hevc-wf-N` (wavefront rows),
    `dec-hevc-lf-N` (loop filters).
